.\" Automatically generated by Pandoc 1.18
.\"
.TH "getServers" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
getServers \- get the server information synchronized by the STP node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]stp.getServers()\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Stp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to get the server information synchronized by the STP
node.
STP node and server group description can refer to logical time.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
None
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, it will return the list of server group
information synchronized by the STP node through the cursor.
Users can refer to stpq query server information to get the returned field
information.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
When the exception happens, use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v5.0 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Get the server information synchronized by the STP node.
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> var stp = new Stp()
> stp.getServers()
{
  "Version": 1,
  "Group": [
    {
      "Role": "server",
      "HostName": "server\-1",
      "Service": "9622"
    }
  ],
  "PrimaryNode": {
    "HostName": "server\-1",
    "Service": "9622"
  }
}
\f[]
.fi
